.TH NOWMTEST 1
.SH NAME
nowmtest \- regression test for the no-window-manager draw context
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nowmtest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Nowmtest
checks that an application started without a window manager can still
build a Tk window and draw into it.
It prints one line per stage and a final
.B PASS
or
.BR "SOME CHECKS FAILED" .
.PP
An application launched with no wm has no
.IR draw (2)
context, and falls back to
.IR wmclient (2)'s
.BR makedrawcontext ,
which returns a context whose
.B wm
channel is
.BR nil .
Real applications do this directly \(em
.I dreammachines/tutor.b
and its siblings all contain
.IB "if(ctxt == nil) ctxt" " = wmclient\->makedrawcontext()" .
.B Nowmtest
walks that same path:
.BR makedrawcontext ,
.IR tkclient (2)'s
.BR toplevel ,
.BR onscreen ,
.BR startinput ,
then widget creation, packing, an update and a resize, checking that
each returns rather than blocking.
It also confirms that nothing arrives on the control channel, and that
waiting for it is not required to make progress.
.PP
Those checks only show that nothing deadlocked.
The one that shows the window is real reads the toplevel's own image
back with
.B readpixels
and counts non-zero bytes, which depends on nothing outside the
process \(em no window server, no accessibility API, and no unlocked
screen, all of which make screenshots an unreliable test on some
hosts.
A 1024x768 toplevel with a single button typically reports around 2.3
of 3.1 million bytes non-zero.
.PP
It needs a graphical backend; under a headless
.IR emu (1)
it exits reporting that no display could be allocated.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/nowmtest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR wmclient (2),
.IR tkclient (2),
.IR tk (2)
.SH BUGS
Tk starts helper processes that would keep the emulator alive after
the test finished, so the test runs in its own process group and takes
it down before exiting.
Killing processes that are blocked reading leaves the emulator
printing a few
.B "rread ... fdtochan failed"
lines after the result.
They are teardown noise, not a failure; the exit status and the
.B PASS
line are the result.
